RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
February 23, 2009
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met on this date beginning at 6:00 p.m. in
Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL MEMBERS - Ms.
Ash, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case, Mr. Collins, Mr. Pierson, Dr. Rinne, Mr. Spiker and
Mr. Valdez.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Bob Mason,
Assistant City Attorney.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to
be routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no
separate discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and
support by two other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be
considered in its normal sequence on the agenda.) Upon request by Mr. Spiker, and pursuant to
support received by Mr. Brown and Mr. Pierson, agenda item #13 was removed from the
Consent Agenda.  It was noted that procedurally members did not need to officially provide a
“second” to a request to remove consent agenda items.  Mr. Spiker moved to approve remaining
Consent Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Collins.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members
of the governing body.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM REGULAR MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
FEBRUARY 9, 2009.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM VOUCHERS MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
FEBRUARY 17, 2009.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Valdez moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr.
Brown.  Mr. Collins and Mr. Valdez each declared a conflict of interest (business interests) and
vacated Council Chambers. Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body
present in Council Chambers.  Following announcement of the vote, Mr. Collins and Mr. Valdez
returned to Council Chambers.
Mayor Kaysen opened and conducted three public hearings for the purpose of receiving
comments and input on the following:
A public hearing to determine whether compliance of annexation conditions required by
Wyo. Stat. §15-1-402 exists for the property described as Lot 5, Block 2,  Seaver’s Subdivision,
Laramie County, WY.  Don Threewitt, Urban Planning Office, reviewed requirements and
compliance of conditions contained in Wyo. Stat. §15-1-402, including specific information
indicating compliance with Wyo. Stat. §15-1-402(a)(i) through (vi). There being no further
comments or input and purpose of the public hearing having been met, Mayor Kaysen closed the
hearing.
