### Page 5 of 7

```text
[CA]
Contract between the City of Cheyenne, Police Department, and PropertyRoom.com,
Inc., a Delaware Corporation, for property disposition services to dispense of unclaimed property
being stored in the evidence room.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried. (#5349)
Professional Services Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and AVI, P.C. for design
services for the Carey Avenue and Pioneer Avenue Rehabilitation Project (2007-2010 1% Sales
Tax).  Mr. Valdez reported there was no recommendation on the item from Finance Committee.
Mr. Collins moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Pierson. Upon inquiry, Bruce Perryman, AVI
Engineering, reviewed elements and approaches the engineering firm would be utilizing in
conjunction with project design services, including communication and assistance to businesses
affected by the project area and anticipated design issues, and provided information on services
to be provided; measures to minimize traffic and disturbance on the streets; AVI’s urban renewal
construction experience and expertise; consulting time contained within the proposal submitted,
and the firm’s role in providing construction management assistance to the City.  Mr. Perryman
further reviewed components of the project regarding underground and surface components,
particularly in this area of downtown, and cost adjustments for streetscape and lighting
components.  Upon inquiry, Doug Vetter, Interim City Engineer, provided information on City
staff project management and inspections responsibilities vs. consultant assistance services to be
provided by AVI, and, in response to query, advised that depending upon the complexity of a
project and staff availability, construction management services for future projects may be able
to be provided by staff.  Discussion followed on the proposal(s) review and selection committee
process involving the recommendation by the committee of a vendor. Upon inquiry, Mr.
Perryman stated it is hoped that most of the work can involve a grind and overlay process but
that each block will have to be evaluated individually to determine whether reconstruction vs. an
overlay technique can be utilized, and discussed use of Presidential stimulus funds, if received,
for streetscaping items.  Upon inquiry regarding aspects involving services provided on a
previous Capitol Avenue reconstruction project, Mr. Perryman reviewed issues affiliated with
the previous project regarding concrete cracking of curb, gutters and bump-outs, and subsequent
design changes.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body. (#5350)
